{title: 282 - I Hear Thy Welcome Voice}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #282 • WELCOME VOICE • 12.14.10.13}
{lyricist: Lewis Hartsough}
{composer: Lewis Hartsough}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 282}
{meta: tune WELCOME VOICE}
{meta: meter 12.14.10.13}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Fm]I hear Thy welcome voice, [Db]That calls me, Lord, to Thee;
[Db/F]For cleansing in Thy precious blood, That flowed on Calvary.
[Ab]I am coming, Lord! [Ab7]Coming now to Thee!
[Ab7]Wash me, cleanse me, in the blood That flowed [Db/Ab]on Calvary.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Ab]I am coming, [Db/Ab]Lord!
[Db/Ab]Coming now to Thee!
[Db]Wash me, cleanse me, in the blood
[Db/Ab]That flowed on Calvary.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Fm]Though coming weak [Db]and vile,
[Db/F]Thou dost my strength assure;
[Ab]Thou dost my vileness [Ab7]fully cleanse,
[Ab7]Till spotless all, [Db/Ab]and pure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Fm]'Tis Jesus [Db]calls me on
[Db/F]To perfect faith and love,
[Ab]To perfect hope, [Ab7]and peace, and trust,
[Ab7]For earth and heaven [Db/Ab]above.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Fm]All hail, atoning [Db/Ab]blood!
[Db/F]All hail, redeeming grace!
[Ab]All hail! the gift [Ab7]of Christ, our Lord,
[Ab7]Our Strength and Righteousness.
{end_of_verse}
